WEBVTT

00:00.490 --> 00:05.500
<b>This is a work of fiction. The names of the people, places, and organizations
are fictitious and in no way related to any real person or entity.</b>

00:01.470 --> 00:03.750
<i>December 31st.</i>

00:03.750 --> 00:05.980
<i>The time is right before midnight.</i>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.700
<b>m 0 0 l 100 0 100 100 0 100</b>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.700
<b>< Shikanoko-san</b>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.700
<b>Let's meet at the bottom of the
stairs at 11:30 PM. Don't be late.</b>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.700
<b>Read
20:13</b>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.700
<b>Roger</b>

00:10.480 --> 00:13.700
<b>Today</b>

00:10.900 --> 00:13.700
Man, Shikanoko's late.

00:11.800 --> 00:13.700
<b>I'm here</b>

00:12.760 --> 00:13.700
<b>Where are you right now?</b>

00:13.470 --> 00:13.700
<b>Hello?</b>

00:13.700 --> 00:33.800
<b>Shikagami Shrine</b>

00:13.930 --> 00:19.410
She's got some nerve inviting me to the first
shrine visit of the year and making me wait.

00:20.570 --> 00:24.010
To think that we get to start off the year 
by swearing our love for each other...

00:24.010 --> 00:26.610
It's going to be a good year.

00:26.610 --> 00:28.540
I'm not swearing anything with you.

00:30.420 --> 00:33.800
Well, whatever. I guess the three 
of us can go pay our respects.

00:39.560 --> 00:41.800
It's almost time for the unveiling!

00:41.800 --> 00:43.070
I can hardly wait!

00:43.070 --> 00:44.880
This only happens once a year, after all!

00:44.880 --> 00:47.450
I wonder if there's some kind of event.

00:47.450 --> 00:49.570
Hey! There're the shrine maidens!

01:09.500 --> 01:11.680
Shikanoko?!

01:11.680 --> 01:15.470
<i>Their first shrine visit of the year, 
and Nokotan's already become a god.</i>

02:46.020 --> 02:51.020
<b>Deer After Deer</b>

02:51.020 --> 02:52.100
Wait, wha—

02:52.100 --> 02:54.880
Shikanoko? The hell are you doing?

02:54.880 --> 02:57.360
Ah, so that's the great Deer God.

02:57.360 --> 02:59.270
This is Bashame's first time seeing her.

02:59.270 --> 03:00.720
Those are some magnificent antlers.

03:00.720 --> 03:02.360
Shikanoko?! A god?!

03:02.610 --> 03:04.870
Also, get a clue, you two!

03:04.870 --> 03:08.340
Is this your first time at this shrine, lass?

03:08.340 --> 03:10.540
Huh? Uh, yes.

03:10.780 --> 03:14.590
Hey! You're that one old lady that's, 
like, a hardcore deer fan!

03:14.590 --> 03:18.120
I am known as the Old Granny of Hino. 
My name is Inukai Mitsu.

03:16.650 --> 03:23.550
<b>Inukai Mitsu (88)</b>

03:18.120 --> 03:20.550
I'm the head priest of this shrine.

03:20.550 --> 03:23.550
A proper self-intro! She's definitely 
eyeing a regular cast position!

03:23.840 --> 03:27.190
She's the god of this Shikagami Shrine

03:27.190 --> 03:30.590
and the symbol of deer prosperity here in Hino.

03:30.590 --> 03:31.950
"Symbol"?

03:31.950 --> 03:35.020
And what's the point of wishing 
for the prosperity of deer in Hino?!

03:35.550 --> 03:39.470
C-Come on. She's clearly 
just a plain ol' deer.

03:39.470 --> 03:42.590
Her, a god? Clearly, there's 
been some kind of mista—

03:42.590 --> 03:45.280
Silence, boy! I mean, girl!

03:47.580 --> 03:50.410
Just go see for yourself.

03:50.800 --> 03:54.420
H-Hey, Shikanoko-san! 
What are you doing there?

03:54.420 --> 03:56.420
Hurry up and come down here!

03:57.520 --> 03:59.670
And quit it with that enlightened look!

03:59.670 --> 04:02.000
Just hurry up and come down here!

04:02.000 --> 04:03.930
One is not "Shikanoko."

04:05.250 --> 04:06.740
One is a deer.

04:06.740 --> 04:07.540
Same difference!

04:07.540 --> 04:09.870
And shouldn't you have said "the Deer God"?!

04:11.680 --> 04:13.820
Oh, such blessed words!

04:13.820 --> 04:16.500
Hino will be protected by the 
Deer God for another year!

04:16.500 --> 04:19.010
We're starting off the 
new year with great luck!

04:19.010 --> 04:21.030
You guys are totally getting duped!

04:21.030 --> 04:23.960
May Bashame get her rice paddy this year!

04:23.960 --> 04:27.570
May I be able to do all kinds of naughty 
things with my sister this year!

04:27.570 --> 04:28.950
Not you two, too!

04:29.390 --> 04:32.130
Damn it. What's with this shrine?

04:32.130 --> 04:35.460
Not only is the god messed up, 
so are all the visitors!

04:37.190 --> 04:42.840
It appears as though you also enjoyed 
our great Deer God's unveiling.

04:42.840 --> 04:45.220
What in the world gave you that idea?

04:45.220 --> 04:48.600
Why don't you take one of our fortune slips?

04:48.970 --> 04:50.350
Fortune slips?

04:50.350 --> 04:55.540
Our Shikagami Shrine fortunes 
are famous for their accuracy.

04:55.540 --> 04:58.480
Huh... Well, if you insist.

04:59.730 --> 05:02.550
I might as well draw a great blessing 
or something else good.

05:02.550 --> 05:03.320
There!

05:04.080 --> 05:05.530
Ooh, I got a...

05:05.530 --> 05:07.320
<b>Shikagami Shrine Fortune</b>

05:05.530 --> 05:07.320
<b>Your
Luck:</b>

05:05.530 --> 05:07.320
<b>GREAT ANTLER</b>

05:07.270 --> 05:08.570
My luck will be what now?!

05:09.800 --> 05:19.670
<b>[Lost Item] Right Antler</b>

05:09.870 --> 05:13.400
You mean I'm going to find my antler?! Even 
though I don't remember ever losing one?!

05:13.270 --> 05:19.670
<b>[Person Waiting For You] A deer</b>

05:13.820 --> 05:17.560
I'm only seeing deer and 
antlers on this damn fortune!

05:17.640 --> 05:19.670
<b>will appear in 3 minutes</b>

05:18.020 --> 05:19.670
It's also so unnecessarily detailed!

05:19.670 --> 05:22.550
I hope I pull a great antler this year.

05:22.550 --> 05:25.490
I'll be content if I get 
an eventual antler or better.

05:25.490 --> 05:27.590
So I'm supposed to treat 
this as a great blessing?

05:28.240 --> 05:30.840
A-A-A-A-A small antler!

05:30.840 --> 05:32.570
Get a grip, Kinu.

05:32.570 --> 05:35.930
Ugh, you're so pathetic. 
It's just a simple fortune.

05:36.150 --> 05:38.150
Oh, hey. You guys are here, too?

05:39.010 --> 05:41.760
President. Happy New Year.

05:41.760 --> 05:45.520
I-I'm so sorry that you had 
to see my disgusting, unlucky,

05:45.520 --> 05:47.870
and unwanted face first thing this year!

05:47.870 --> 05:50.090
I-I'm not here to make a new year's resolution

05:50.090 --> 05:53.950
to finally do something about 
the Deer Club or anything.

05:53.950 --> 05:55.200
<b>Fortune</b>

05:53.950 --> 05:55.200
<b>GREAT
MIS-FAWN-TUNE</b>

05:57.090 --> 05:59.220
I need to get rid of this immediately!

06:04.670 --> 06:06.840
Are you all right, Vice President?

06:06.840 --> 06:08.760
P-P-Please don't cry!

06:08.760 --> 06:11.450
Ouchies, ouchies, fly away!

06:11.450 --> 06:14.780
Are you mocking me just because I'm small?!

06:14.780 --> 06:16.670
N-N-No, I didn't mean it like that...

06:16.670 --> 06:19.030
Now, now. Let's go tie up our fortunes.

06:22.180 --> 06:23.370
<i>She's so cute...</i>

06:24.530 --> 06:27.710
Hm? I smell something sweet.

06:27.710 --> 06:29.080
Child of man.

06:30.270 --> 06:32.620
One shall bestow a serving unto you.

06:32.620 --> 06:34.940
Come closer.

06:34.640 --> 06:37.250
<b>Reset</b>

06:34.640 --> 06:37.250
<b>Start</b>

06:34.760 --> 06:37.250
<b>[Person Waiting For You]
A deer will appear in 3 minutes</b>

06:34.940 --> 06:37.250
Exactly three minutes! 
It actually predicted the future!

06:37.740 --> 06:43.130
Shikanoko, you ass! You've got some 
nerve breaking your promise with me.

06:43.450 --> 06:47.670
You handin' out amazake 
after playing god? Huh?

06:47.670 --> 06:48.380
Nay.

06:48.900 --> 06:50.240
This is antler soup.

06:50.240 --> 06:52.160
The hell is antler soup?

06:52.590 --> 06:54.130
Soup of antler.

06:54.130 --> 06:57.110
You didn't explain a damn thing! 
There's no way I'm drinking that stuff!

06:57.110 --> 06:59.390
Also seriously, what's with that face?!

06:59.390 --> 07:03.300
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:03.300 --> 07:06.950
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:04.150 --> 07:09.990
<i>Antler soup is a soup bestowed 
upon us humans by the Deer God</i>

07:07.250 --> 07:10.830
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:09.990 --> 07:11.260
<i>every year at New Year's.</i>

07:11.260 --> 07:12.280
That sounds shady as hell!

07:12.540 --> 07:16.220
<i>The Deer God herself becomes the stock 
and doesn't sleep for three days</i>

07:16.220 --> 07:18.470
<i>and three nights as this 
extremely blessed drink</i>

07:18.470 --> 07:20.790
<i>is created in the cellar of this shrine.</i>

07:21.190 --> 07:22.720
What does any of that even mean?!

07:22.720 --> 07:24.920
So it's created by literally stewing her?!

07:24.920 --> 07:26.850
Like hell I'm gonna drink that!

07:28.190 --> 07:28.920
Huh?

07:29.150 --> 07:33.320
O Great Deer God, it is almost time.

07:33.320 --> 07:34.700
Time?

07:37.590 --> 07:41.060
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:41.060 --> 07:45.310
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:45.310 --> 07:49.090
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:45.910 --> 07:47.980
<i>The hell is this bizarre ritual?</i>

07:47.980 --> 07:49.490
<i>Also, aren't you supposed to burn</i>

07:49.090 --> 07:53.310
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:49.490 --> 07:51.710
<i>last year's ceremonial arrows 
in these ceremonial fires?</i>

07:51.710 --> 07:53.700
<i>Why the hell are you burning antlers?!</i>

07:53.310 --> 07:57.040
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:53.930 --> 07:56.620
They're going all out for 
this year's ceremonial fire.

07:56.620 --> 07:58.410
You're telling me they do this every year?

07:57.260 --> 08:01.580
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

07:58.430 --> 08:00.690
I think we're going to 
be extra lucky this year.

08:00.690 --> 08:01.580
Yeah, no!

08:01.580 --> 08:04.420
May we have huge harvests 
and a year of full harvests!

08:04.420 --> 08:06.770
Bring on the debauchery! All the debauchery!

08:06.770 --> 08:08.210
Seriously, you guys...

08:09.930 --> 08:14.760
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

08:12.310 --> 08:13.610
What's with the wind?!

08:13.610 --> 08:14.760
Hey! Look!

08:14.990 --> 08:17.050
The Deer God started shining!

08:17.050 --> 08:18.010
Why, though?!

08:18.010 --> 08:21.520
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

08:21.840 --> 08:25.740
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

08:25.740 --> 08:29.990
Eenie, meenie, miney, doe!

08:35.410 --> 08:37.410
Notsu...

08:43.410 --> 08:46.230
Oh, blessed be! Blessed be!

08:46.230 --> 08:47.880
Who, what, where, how, why?!

08:50.550 --> 08:52.640
That was pretty fun.

08:52.640 --> 08:56.820
It feels like this is going to be a 
good year. Right, Koshitan-senpai?

08:57.480 --> 09:00.860
Ugh, the new year only just started, 
and I'm already friggin' exhausted.

09:00.860 --> 09:02.810
I'm heading right home and warming up.

09:03.400 --> 09:05.020
Oh, hey! Koshitan!

09:05.690 --> 09:07.450
Sorry to keep you waiting!

09:08.430 --> 09:10.630
Ah, Nokotan-senpai.

09:10.630 --> 09:13.630
You jerk! Not only do you make me wait,

09:13.630 --> 09:16.310
you go and pull that Deer God act 
with the ceremonial fires and stuff!

09:16.310 --> 09:18.210
I'm heading home, damn it!

09:18.640 --> 09:19.700
What do you mean?

09:19.700 --> 09:21.780
I just got here.

09:21.780 --> 09:22.830
What?!

09:22.830 --> 09:26.580
But I'm really sorry if I made you wait. 
You must've been really cold.

09:26.580 --> 09:29.310
Here, drink some of this and warm up.

09:29.310 --> 09:31.070
Huh? Uh, sure...

09:31.070 --> 09:33.090
I have some for you two, too.

09:33.930 --> 09:35.430
Wow, that's delicious!

09:35.430 --> 09:36.940
That hit the spot.

09:38.570 --> 09:41.850
Yum... I've never had 
this before. What is it?

09:43.080 --> 09:43.760
Antler soup.

09:43.760 --> 09:46.480
So it <i>was</i> you up there!

09:48.500 --> 09:53.480
<b>I'll make sure the
Deer Club makes its mark!
-Koshi Torako</b>

09:48.500 --> 09:53.480
<b>I'm gonna become
Hino's local mascot!!
-Nokotan</b>

09:48.500 --> 09:53.480
<b>I'm gonna do naughty
things with my sister
-Koshi Anko</b>

09:48.500 --> 09:53.480
<b>Bashame will become a
great deer and eat rice
-Bashame</b>

09:49.870 --> 09:52.780
<i>After that, we all did our 
first shrine visit together.</i>

09:53.480 --> 09:56.990
<b>Kanagawa Prefecture
 Oyama Afuri Shrine</b>

09:56.990 --> 10:00.490
<b>Kanagawa Prefecture
 Oyama Afuri Shrine</b>

10:00.790 --> 10:03.580
Happy New Year to you all.

10:03.580 --> 10:05.900
And here we go with this 
indigenous god thing.

10:07.120 --> 10:15.010
<b>Happy New Deer</b>

10:07.340 --> 10:13.010
We hope that you'll continue to support 
<i>My Deer Friend Nokotan</i> this year, too.

10:13.010 --> 10:15.010
Th-Thanks...

10:15.010 --> 10:16.700
With that, here.

10:16.700 --> 10:17.760
Here what?

10:18.460 --> 10:20.510
Gimme New Year's money.

10:20.510 --> 10:22.680
If you're a god, don't pester me for money!

10:24.180 --> 10:27.640
I think that's enough New Year's jokes.

10:34.010 --> 10:37.470
Okay, let's get the actual show started!

10:34.730 --> 10:40.240
<b>Happy New Deer</b>

10:37.470 --> 10:40.260
The hell was up with that 
rando New Year's greeting?

10:40.260 --> 10:44.740
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

10:45.410 --> 10:47.500
Well? Are you all ready?

10:49.940 --> 10:53.060
<i>One of the traditions for New Year's 
is playing a board game.</i>

10:53.620 --> 10:56.800
<i>There are countless games that span 
across all ages and many places,</i>

10:56.800 --> 11:00.800
<i>but did you know that one particular 
game is the most popular?</i>

11:02.470 --> 11:07.290
<i>Its groundbreaking setup caused a huge 
sensation when it was first released.</i>

11:07.290 --> 11:09.800
<i>Yes, it's the game you're all familiar with:</i>

11:10.500 --> 11:12.400
<b>Game of Deer Life
Deluxe</b>

11:10.630 --> 11:12.400
<i>the Game of Deer Life.</i>

11:13.400 --> 11:16.460
I'm not gonna go easy on ya 
just cuz this is a board game.

11:16.460 --> 11:21.280
I'll show you exactly what 
it means to compete with me!

11:21.340 --> 11:22.780
<b>The Beast of Hino
Roars Into the Fight!!</b>

11:23.160 --> 11:23.910
<b>An</b>

11:25.120 --> 11:29.060
Since we're competing, this means 
we're wagering something, too, right?

11:29.060 --> 11:31.520
Your livelihood, your chastity, your life...

11:31.520 --> 11:33.750
Ooh, I'm getting excited!

11:33.750 --> 11:35.290
<b>The Out-of-Control Siscon
Creeps In!!</b>

11:36.660 --> 11:37.890
Pitiful!

11:37.890 --> 11:41.030
You humans just keep yapping.

11:41.030 --> 11:42.400
I'll show you what a true deer...

11:43.720 --> 11:45.290
can do.

11:45.290 --> 11:46.810
<b>An Actual Deer
Leaps Into the Fray!!</b>

11:47.350 --> 11:51.810
<i>The First-Ever Chitty Chitty Hino High School 
Deer Club Game of Deer Life Tournament!</i>

11:51.810 --> 11:54.560
<i>Let the games begin!</i>

11:54.560 --> 11:55.810
Start!

11:56.190 --> 11:58.580
Okay, I'll go first.

11:58.580 --> 11:59.190
Go!

12:02.070 --> 12:04.200
<b>Start</b>

12:02.070 --> 12:04.200
<b>Born in the Hino Zoo!</b>

12:02.470 --> 12:04.370
I guess I'm moving four spaces.

12:04.370 --> 12:07.940
One, two, three, four.

12:07.940 --> 12:09.450
Huh? What's going on?

12:09.680 --> 12:12.660
Ah, a newborn deer!

12:12.660 --> 12:15.360
Here, to celebrate!

12:15.360 --> 12:19.210
<i>Become friends with the zookeeper. 
Receive three stacks of deer crackers.</i>

12:19.580 --> 12:22.970
<i>The currency in the Game of Deer Life 
is not money but deer crackers.</i>

12:23.350 --> 12:27.950
<i>The one with the most deer crackers 
at the end of the game wins.</i>

12:27.950 --> 12:29.800
Hey, this is a great start.

12:29.800 --> 12:30.970
No fair.

12:30.970 --> 12:32.590
<i>Now, it's Koshitan's turn.</i>

12:32.590 --> 12:35.050
All right! I'm up next!

12:36.570 --> 12:37.980
Ooh, a nine!

12:37.980 --> 12:40.870
I'm gonna keep on truckin' 
and get to the goal!

12:41.460 --> 12:42.230
Hm?

12:42.230 --> 12:45.560
Aren't you being a bit cocky 
just because you're younger?

12:45.560 --> 12:47.900
Whose turf do you think you're on? Huh?

12:47.900 --> 12:50.740
Don't think you can stay here for free!

12:50.970 --> 12:51.870
Huh?

12:52.530 --> 12:57.640
<i>Tormented by senpai deer and shaken down 
for deer crackers. Hand over thirty.</i>

12:57.640 --> 12:59.620
Give us all you've got!

12:59.620 --> 13:02.010
Isn't this a bit harsh right off the bat?!

13:02.010 --> 13:05.930
Also, I don't even have any 
deer crackers to give yet.

13:05.930 --> 13:07.720
Over here, lassie.

13:07.720 --> 13:08.550
Huh?

13:09.160 --> 13:11.430
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

13:09.660 --> 13:11.430
<b>Interest
50%</b>

13:09.800 --> 13:11.430
Come on.

13:11.430 --> 13:26.950
<b>Interest
50%</b>

13:11.430 --> 13:26.950
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

13:11.430 --> 13:26.950
<b>Deer Crackers</b>

13:11.960 --> 13:13.370
Pleasure doin' business with ya.

13:14.470 --> 13:17.870
<i>When you don't have enough deer crackers, 
the zoo will lend you some.</i>

13:17.870 --> 13:19.870
<i>The interest rate is 50%!</i>

13:19.870 --> 13:23.460
The zoo and these senpai deer 
are totally working together...

13:23.460 --> 13:26.950
I guess survival of the fittest 
applies to herbivores, too.

13:28.480 --> 13:30.380
You just don't get it, Koshitan.

13:30.380 --> 13:31.080
Wha?

13:31.080 --> 13:34.010
The key to the Game of Deer Life 
isn't how fast you can reach the goal

13:34.010 --> 13:37.330
but how many deer crackers you can amass!

13:37.330 --> 13:39.710
Therefore, even if it takes longer,

13:39.710 --> 13:44.410
you've gotta aim for the spaces 
that'll give you more deer crackers!

13:44.410 --> 13:45.820
<i>Nokotan's turn.</i>

13:45.820 --> 13:49.740
<i>She's escaped the zoo, wandered 
into the neighborhood, and...</i>

13:50.800 --> 13:53.070
<i>ended up hanging off some electrical lines.</i>

13:53.070 --> 13:54.480
<i>Lose one turn.</i>

13:55.350 --> 13:56.180
Déjà vu!

13:56.410 --> 13:58.190
<i>Also, while she was hanging there,</i>

13:58.190 --> 14:02.490
<i>she was attacked by vultures and hyenas, 
losing fifty deer crackers.</i>

14:02.490 --> 14:03.820
Doe no!

14:03.820 --> 14:06.700
Sometimes, this is harsher than reality.

14:06.930 --> 14:08.730
<i>It's once again Anko's turn.</i>

14:08.730 --> 14:11.030
One, two, three.

14:11.030 --> 14:12.580
Okay, now...

14:15.190 --> 14:18.820
Don't be afraid. Now, jump into my arms!

14:18.820 --> 14:20.960
Oh, but I'm a virgin...

14:23.850 --> 14:27.040
<i>A deer you've had feelings for 
mates with another female deer.</i>

14:23.980 --> 14:29.590
<b>*Visuals may differ from actual events</b>

14:27.040 --> 14:29.590
<i>The shock leaves you bedridden. Lose one turn.</i>

14:29.590 --> 14:30.860
Oh, my.

14:30.860 --> 14:33.260
Hey! This depiction's pretty malicious!

14:33.570 --> 14:37.160
This actually happened 
at my workplace recently.

14:37.160 --> 14:39.000
Wait, really? Do you work in a soap opera?

14:39.000 --> 14:41.350
I guess deer have a lot going on, too.

14:43.070 --> 14:47.020
But if the shock from that leaves them bedridden, 
I'd say their love just isn't enough.

14:47.020 --> 14:48.400
What do you mean?

14:48.780 --> 14:52.310
If it were me, I'd whip, whip them 
over and over, then slap, slap them,

14:52.310 --> 14:55.730
squish, squish them, and in the end, 
I'd mlem, mlem them...

14:55.730 --> 14:58.370
I'm just going to pretend 
I never heard that, okay?

14:58.370 --> 15:00.000
<i>It's now Koshitan's turn.</i>

15:00.000 --> 15:01.670
Okay, next is...

15:01.670 --> 15:03.600
<i>A sudden growth spurt!</i>

15:03.600 --> 15:06.820
<i>Spin the roulette, and gain antlers 
equal to the number you roll!</i>

15:06.820 --> 15:08.210
Where am I gaining them?!

15:10.950 --> 15:13.220
The highest number now, of all times!

15:13.660 --> 15:18.200
<i>In celebration, also receive the same number 
of deer crackers from each player.</i>

15:18.200 --> 15:20.280
I mean, I'm thankful for that, but...

15:27.230 --> 15:30.540
I look like I've been riddled with arrows...

15:30.540 --> 15:32.020
Here're your deer crackers.

15:32.020 --> 15:34.620
Are you celebrating or commiserating?

15:34.620 --> 15:36.170
<i>It's now Nokotan's turn.</i>

15:37.540 --> 15:38.750
<i>Lose one turn.</i>

15:40.250 --> 15:42.870
The rice is looking great!

15:43.700 --> 15:45.500
<i>And the game proceeded onward.</i>

15:48.510 --> 15:50.880
Deer life decisions?

15:48.510 --> 15:50.880
<b><u>Intense Course</u></b>

15:48.510 --> 15:50.880
<b>Intense Course</b>

15:48.510 --> 15:50.880
<b><u>Stable Course</u></b>

15:48.510 --> 15:50.880
<b>Stable Course</b>

15:48.510 --> 15:50.880
<b>Stop!
Deer Life Decisions</b>

15:52.520 --> 15:54.430
<i>You're on your own after leaving the zoo!</i>

15:54.430 --> 15:57.640
<i>As the harsh waves of society crash over you, 
you'll hold on for deer life</i>

15:57.640 --> 15:59.650
<i>in the Intense course.</i>

16:00.260 --> 16:03.900
<i>Alternatively, you can stay at the zoo, 
passing up any great changes or promotions</i>

16:03.900 --> 16:08.360
<i>in exchange for a safe and predictable life 
on the Stable course.</i>

16:08.360 --> 16:10.680
<i>Which will you choose?</i>

16:09.710 --> 16:12.240
<b>Intense</b>

16:09.710 --> 16:12.240
<b>Stable</b>

16:11.080 --> 16:12.240
This is just life.

16:12.240 --> 16:14.840
By the way, if you select the Intense course,

16:14.840 --> 16:18.340
you get to choose from the 
mountains, sea, or city.

16:18.340 --> 16:19.500
Hm...

16:19.500 --> 16:23.290
Then I guess I'll choose the Intense course 
of deer life and head to the mountains.

16:23.620 --> 16:28.500
I'll conquer the mountains and shake down 
all the deer there for their deer crackers.

16:28.500 --> 16:31.830
I think you might be more cut out 
to be a delinquent than I am.

16:31.830 --> 16:34.470
In that case, I guess 
I'll head into the city!

16:34.470 --> 16:37.010
I'll gradually climb the ranks of my career!

16:37.010 --> 16:38.050
What about you, Shikanoko?

16:38.050 --> 16:41.690
Someone is calling for me in a faraway land.

16:41.690 --> 16:43.030
I can feel it.

16:43.030 --> 16:43.810
So the sea.

16:43.810 --> 16:44.780
Yup, the sea.

16:50.440 --> 16:53.180
The dawn in Hino City draws near!

17:03.580 --> 17:06.150
<i>Nokotan crossed the sea...</i>

17:06.900 --> 17:09.020
<i>and washed ashore in Alaska.</i>

17:09.020 --> 17:10.460
Why Alaska, though?!

17:14.340 --> 17:16.840
<i>Oh? Something strange 
is happening to Nokotan.</i>

17:20.130 --> 17:23.740
<i>Congratulations! 
Nokotan has evolved into a moose.</i>

17:22.620 --> 17:25.600
<b>Current total number
of deer crackers: 100</b>

17:24.370 --> 17:25.600
How does any of that work?!

17:26.040 --> 17:29.480
This is definitely an intense deer life.

17:29.910 --> 17:31.400
She's actually evolved in real life!

17:32.630 --> 17:36.740
Now that I've evolved into the highest 
class of deer, the moose, that means...

17:36.740 --> 17:38.420
I get bonus deer cra—

17:38.420 --> 17:39.720
<i>You don't actually get anything.</i>

17:40.800 --> 17:43.760
Aw, I guess you're not so special, 
even if you are an actual deer.

17:43.760 --> 17:46.660
How dare you?! Then what about you, Koshian?

17:48.380 --> 17:52.590
<i>She gradually took over the mountain and 
made all the animals her subordinates.</i>

17:52.820 --> 17:57.340
<i>She calls it a tip, but she makes them 
all pay her ten deer crackers a day.</i>

17:57.340 --> 18:00.580
Those who defy me will get 
what's coming to them.

17:57.340 --> 18:01.850
<b>Current total number
of deer crackers: 103,000</b>

18:00.580 --> 18:01.850
Ruling by fear?!

18:02.150 --> 18:04.100
I get all the deer crackers I want to eat.

18:04.100 --> 18:05.010
No fair!

18:05.010 --> 18:07.800
Heh. You've still got a 
long ways to go, Anko.

18:07.800 --> 18:08.980
What do you mean by that?

18:13.860 --> 18:15.910
Look this way, please!

18:15.910 --> 18:16.740
Sure!

18:17.590 --> 18:20.240
<b>Bronze @bronze_dolota
One in a hundred million deer shot
#NaraPark</b>

18:19.910 --> 18:23.490
Just like that! Nice! Very good!

18:25.430 --> 18:27.750
<b>Matsu @take_nara_1980
A miraculous beauty deer born from Hino</b>

18:25.430 --> 18:27.750
<b>Noah. @noah22
She's too beautiful...!</b>

18:28.330 --> 18:32.600
<i>After a famous photographer's pics of her 
go viral, she becomes a Nara Park idol.</i>

18:32.600 --> 18:38.320
<i>Due to her ever-increasing audience, Koshitan 
collects 100 deer crackers per space moved.</i>

18:38.640 --> 18:43.140
Your pocket change ain't got nothin' on me!

18:40.950 --> 18:43.890
<b>Current total number of
deer crackers: 30,000,000</b>

18:43.890 --> 18:48.630
I'm gonna wring all those tourists dry 
and quit while I'm ahead!

18:50.020 --> 18:54.380
I didn't expect a former delinquent 
like you would be into idols.

18:54.380 --> 18:57.200
My sister's pretty interested in 
girly things, despite how she looks.

18:57.200 --> 18:58.560
Shut your mouths!

18:58.560 --> 19:00.230
This is just a game!

19:00.230 --> 19:03.320
<i>Koshitan didn't actually hate this.</i>

19:05.790 --> 19:07.430
<i>It's now Nokotan's turn.</i>

19:10.670 --> 19:12.850
Ah, so it's my turn.

19:12.850 --> 19:14.820
You seem like a completely 
different character...

19:14.820 --> 19:16.210
<i>Some trouble ahead!</i>

19:17.050 --> 19:19.530
<i>An incredibly violent grizzly has appeared.</i>

19:19.530 --> 19:21.930
<i>Nokotan's life is on the line!</i>

19:23.010 --> 19:27.060
I guess the reason I grew these 
antlers was for this day.

19:45.370 --> 19:46.910
With this, Alaska—

19:46.910 --> 19:50.060
no, America has finally attained freedom.

19:50.460 --> 19:52.620
The hell happened to you, Grizzly?!

19:52.620 --> 19:57.510
<i>As a token of thanks, the American president, 
the American citizens,</i>

19:57.510 --> 20:01.130
<i>and the animals living in America 
give you 50 million deer crackers.</i>

20:01.130 --> 20:04.100
May the antlers be with you.

20:04.100 --> 20:06.140
Dude, your antlers are way too OP!

20:06.380 --> 20:08.640
Rolly, rolly them all round.

20:09.040 --> 20:11.020
<i>And the game continued to advance.</i>

20:12.770 --> 20:17.120
Guess you guys needed another hundred 
years if you actually wanted to beat me!

20:17.120 --> 20:21.790
While you two were dawdling, 
I've been raking in 200 billion a year.

20:21.790 --> 20:28.060
I evolved into a super-elite idol deer, and 
my total assets equal over 1,600,000,000!

20:28.430 --> 20:29.660
When'd she manage that?

20:29.660 --> 20:31.000
Well done, Onee-chan.

20:31.000 --> 20:34.400
Now I'm gonna run straight for the goal!

20:34.920 --> 20:39.340
Hello! We're doing a photoshoot 
for my new photobook, right?

20:39.980 --> 20:44.080
I-I-I'm so sorry! I promise 
I don't know anything!

20:45.150 --> 20:47.680
Um, so I heard that...

20:48.610 --> 20:49.810
Koshi-san...

20:49.810 --> 20:51.680
You're not actually a deer.

20:53.200 --> 21:02.440
<b>The Shocking Scoop</b>

20:53.200 --> 21:03.280
<b>Popular Idol Deer
Falsified Her Past?!</b>

20:55.060 --> 20:56.770
Wait, what the hell is this?!

20:56.770 --> 20:58.240
A scandal comes to light!

20:58.240 --> 21:02.440
The popular idol wasn't actually 
a deer! She was a capybara!

21:03.160 --> 21:04.950
There's no way in hell!

21:05.210 --> 21:07.170
<i>You end up having to pay 
a fortune in reparations!</i>

21:07.170 --> 21:08.930
<i>You lose your life savings.</i>

21:08.930 --> 21:09.750
Huh?

21:11.490 --> 21:13.790
Ugh! I lost!

21:11.850 --> 21:13.790
<b>Last Place: 0 crackers</b>

21:13.850 --> 21:21.250
<b>1st Place: 62 million crackers</b>

21:13.850 --> 21:21.250
<b>2nd Place: 58 million crackers</b>

21:14.050 --> 21:16.150
Yay, I won!

21:16.150 --> 21:19.290
That last space! If only that 
last space didn't exist!

21:19.290 --> 21:21.250
I guess I just couldn't beat America.

21:22.990 --> 21:25.670
Well, anyway. That was way more 
exciting than I thought it'd be.

21:25.670 --> 21:27.260
And it was pretty fun, too.

21:29.640 --> 21:31.800
Man, I'm starving, though.

21:31.800 --> 21:33.300
I've got some deer crackers.

21:33.300 --> 21:34.860
Yeah, I'm good on those.

21:34.860 --> 21:38.350
By the way, wasn't Bashame 
making some mochi...

21:41.100 --> 21:42.290
Bashame?!

21:43.090 --> 21:46.080
Ah... So she ate too many pieces of mochi, 
and now she's choking.

21:46.080 --> 21:47.240
Unconcerned much?!

21:47.500 --> 21:49.870
Hurry up and spit it out, damn it!

21:49.870 --> 21:51.310
Thaf's sufh a wafte...

21:51.310 --> 21:53.030
Now's not the time for that!

21:55.500 --> 21:57.230
Om, nom, nom...

21:58.670 --> 22:00.750
Whew, that was delicious.

22:01.430 --> 22:02.130
Notsu.

22:02.130 --> 22:04.510
Again, your damn antlers are way too OP!
